  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "spotlight",
      "item": "tribalpower:summoning_cradle",
      "text": [
        "Call living spirits without hunting for them. A Binding Effigy remembers one creature without harming it; a Summoning Cradle then calls that creature up, again and again, while it has Pulse and Spiritweave.",
        "The binding is a ritual, on purpose. It is not a spawn-egg shortcut."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Imprinting an effigy",
      "text": [
        "Craft an empty **Binding Effigy**, then crouch and right-click an eligible creature with it. The creature is not hurt.",
        "Cows, sheep, pigs, chickens, zombies, skeletons, spiders, creepers and the **thirteen** Tribal Power creatures can be imprinted. Bosses cannot.",
        "A live binding cannot be overwritten; spend its threads first. The tooltip names the imprint and the threads left.",
        "An imprint alone has no summons. It must be woven through the three-voice binding."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "The three-voice binding",
      "text": [
        "Seat a **Spirit Seal** in a Ritual Brazier. Place **Earth**, **Air** and **Spirit** totems within 8 blocks, have **200 Pulse** within reach, and carry **three Spiritweave**.",
        "With no redstone on the brazier, right-click it with your imprinted, empty effigy. The three voices knot **512** summoning threads into it, taking the Pulse and the Spiritweave.",
        "An exhausted effigy is renewed the same way, or you can first imprint a different creature onto it.",
        "If something is missing, the brazier says so."
      ]
    },
